      "experiment_id": "exp_1",
      "description": "Optimized quantum circuit for the call option payoff function f_K(S)=max(S-K,0), including the subtraction stage S-K and the reversible max-with-zero output stage. The paper presents two subtraction implementations (with and without an ancilla qubit) and two payoff implementations (space-efficient and time-efficient), but no runtime experiments on hardware are reported; this is a resource-estimation study.",
      "algorithm": {
        "family": "other-gate-based",
        "variant": "quantum circuit implementation of call option payoff function; two's-complement subtraction with reversible max(S-K,0) output; compared across Cuccaro, Draper, Takahashi, Gidney, and Higher Radix adders",
        "ansatz": null,
        "optimizer": null,
        "num_layers": null,
